{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773252158,"nonce":"yAamrLFkszc7Vr/6+RRj+GRrSDI=","title":"DRY: consolidate Telegram notifications, add project name prefix","message":"Two separate Telegram notification paths exist, violating DRY:\n\n1. **Watcher** (`host/watcher.py`) — `_tg_notify`, `_tg_send_question`, `_tg_ack` with `[project]` prefix\n2. **TelegramNotifier** (`adapters/notifiers/telegram.py`) — `notify`, `send_question` without project prefix\n\nContainer-sent notifications (e.g. \"🏁 done\" from `core/session.py:318`) go through TelegramNotifier and lack the project name, so the user cannot tell which repo a notification is from.\n\nAdditionally, `adapters/notifiers/telegram.py:43` has `except requests.RequestException: pass` — a silent exception catch that violates CLAUDE.md.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `PROJECT_NAME` env var:\n- `host/launch.py`: pass `-e PROJECT_NAME={repo.name}` to Docker\n- `adapters/notifiers/telegram.py`: read `PROJECT_NAME` from env, prefix all messages with `[project]`\n- Fix the silent exception on line 43: log the error\n\nAlso check `adapters/notifiers/webhook.py` and `composite.py` for the same missing prefix and silent catches.\n\n## Files\n- `host/launch.py` — add PROJECT_NAME env var\n- `adapters/notifiers/telegram.py` — add prefix, fix silent catch\n- `adapters/notifiers/webhook.py` — check for same issues\n- `adapters/notifiers/composite.py` — check for same issues\n- `core/session.py` — no changes needed if notifier handles prefix","files":null}]}